course: dictionary
lesson: 3160
title: Context clues and a cheese with holes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easy to picture once you read the words around them. Look for examples, such as the word «like». «Only some cheeses, like Emmental, have holes.» The word «like» shows that Emmental is one example of cheeses with holes, so it must be a kind of cheese.
explain: Look for clues about what a thing is like. «Emmental has a mild, nutty taste and melts well.» Mild means not strong, and nutty tells you the taste is a little like nuts. Melts well tells you why cooks put it in sandwiches and fondue.
explain: Always check your guess. Swap your meaning into the sentence. If «Emmental is a yellow Swiss cheese with big round holes» still makes sense in the story, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Emmental is a yellow cheese from Switzerland with big round holes.
fact: Emmental has a mild, nutty taste and melts well, so it is used in sandwiches and fondue.
fact: Emmental is also called Emmentaler or Emmenthal, and people often call it Swiss cheese.
fact: The holes are made by gas bubbles from tiny bacteria while the cheese ripens.
fact: Only some cheeses, like Emmental, have holes; many cheeses have none at all.
exercise: «Only some cheeses, like Emmental, have holes.» What is Emmental? | *A yellow Swiss cheese with big round holes | A kind of bread | A cheese with big round holes in it | A type of cartoon
exercise: «Tiny bacteria blow gas bubbles into the cheese.» What makes the holes in Emmental? | Holes cut out with a knife | Mice that nibble the cheese | Air blown in by a machine | *Gas bubbles from tiny bacteria
exercise: «Only a few cheeses, like Swiss Emmental, have holes.» Find and copy one word that tells you Emmental is from Switzerland. | Only | *Swiss | Holes | Cheeses
test: Emmental has a mild, nutty taste. Which word tells you it is not strong? | *Mild | Nutty | Taste | Emmental
test: Why is Emmental used in fondue? | Because it is hard and cannot melt | Because it is blue | Because it has no taste at all | *Because it melts well
exam: Jayden says all cheese has round holes like Emmental. Why is he wrong? | Holes are cut into every cheese by a machine | *Only a few cheeses, like Emmental, have holes | Cheese never has holes | Emmental has no holes at all
